EDMS: High-Scale Endpoint Management System
Industrial-Grade Backend for 100K+ Endpoints
This project implements a high-performance documentation and testing ecosystem (similar to Postman/Swagger) designed to manage metadata for over 100,000 endpoints with zero-lock concurrency.

System Architecture
The system follows a Multiprocessing "Pass-Through" Model. Instead of a single monolithic process, we delegate heavy operations (Zip/Merge/Import) to independent worker executables. This prevents data-lock overhead and ensures the main webserver remains responsive under 10k+ user load.

Features & Implementations
1. Adaptive Execution (ZipOps)
The core of our ZipOps (Import, Export, Merge) uses a "Threshold-based Dispatcher" to decide between blocking and non-blocking execution:

Synchronous (Blocking): If the target collection size is below the 50MB Threshold, the handler processes the request immediately for minimal latency.

Asynchronous (Non-Blocking): For high-volume collections (approaching 100k endpoints), the system spawns an external process, returns a TaskID, and logs the PID (Process ID).

2. SQLite Concurrency Manager
To serve 100k endpoints, we implemented a custom RW Lock:

Read Set: Allows massive concurrent read-only access for endpoint testing.

Write Queue: A FIFO (First-In-First-Out) VecDeque manages database writes to prevent the "Database is Locked" error common in SQLite.

3. Scalable Markdown Exporter
To avoid repository bloat and UI lag:

CAP Theorem Partitioning: Data is split into 1,000-record chunks.

Flat Storage Strategy: Automatic generation of paginated files (e.g., endpoints-001.md ... endpoints-100.md).

Project Structure & Handlers
src/main.rs: Orchestrator & Environment Health Checker.

src/sqlite_manager.rs: Concurrency/Lock logic.

src/exporter.rs: Markdown transformation logic.

src/zip_handlers.rs: Core ZipOps implementation including:

export_collection_zip: Recursive directory walking and relative path compression.

get_dir_size: Predictive size estimation for adaptive execution.

set_active_session: Atomic YAML configuration updates to switch endpoint environments.

src/models.rs: Serde-powered IPC (Inter-Process Communication) contracts.

Concurrency & Limits
The system maintains stability via a Throttling Queue:

Concurrency Guard: Limits a single user to 10 concurrent endpoint executions.

Task Lifecycle: Transitions tasks through Queued → Processing(PID) → Completed.

Future-Proofing: Async/Await patterns are used throughout to prepare for QUIC protocol adoption.

Execution (Dockerized)
1. Build and Mount
PowerShell
docker build -t rust-edms .
docker run -d --name edms-container -v "${PWD}:/usr/src/app" rust-edms
2. Run the Dispatcher
PowerShell
# Triggers the environment check and initiates current handlers
docker exec -it edms-container cargo run

Design Philosophy
UI <> Webserver <> Ext-Compute: Strict separation of concerns.

Efficiency: Iterators and io::copy streaming ensure low RAM usage even when zipping 100k files.

Resilience: Using separate PIDs for compute-heavy tasks ensures that a worker crash never brings down the main server.